# How to cite OMICohort. Read by GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and by
# citation managers, so the fields here are the ones a reader will actually get
# handed -- they have to agree with the About tab, which R/about.R renders from
# ABOUT_PEOPLE / ABOUT_LICENSE. tests/test_release_files.R holds the two equal.
#
# `preferred-citation` is deliberately absent: there is no paper yet, and a CFF
# that points at one would be a citation to something that does not exist. When
# there is one, fill ABOUT_CITATION$doi in R/about.R FIRST -- the About page and
# this file both derive from that decision, and the test will demand this file
# catch up rather than let the two drift.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OMICohort, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "OMICohort"
abstract: >-
  A survival-analysis tool for asking whether a molecular score predicts outcome
  across 53 patient cohorts in 7 cancer types. Each cohort is fitted on its own
  with a continuous per-standard-deviation Cox model and the results are combined
  by random-effects meta-analysis, never merged into a single pool. The score
  queried need not be a gene's expression: regulon activity inferred from an
  ARACNe network is a first-class query, which lets a transcription factor be
  assessed by whether its regulatory programme is switched on rather than by its
  own mRNA level.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Korkmaz-Lab/OMICohort"
version: "0.1.2"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
keywords:
  - survival analysis
  - meta-analysis
  - transcription factor
  - regulon
  - VIPER
  - ARACNe
  - cancer genomics
authors:
  - given-names: "Arda Burak"
    family-names: "Karagöz"
    affiliation: "Korkmaz Lab, KUTTAM, Koç University"
    email: "ardaveritas@gmail.com"
  - given-names: "Gözde"
    family-names: "Korkmaz"
    affiliation: "Korkmaz Lab, KUTTAM, Koç University"

# Reference data whose licences make attribution a CONDITION rather than a
# courtesy. These are the non-cohort inputs; the patient cohorts are credited on
# the About tab, where each one's own terms are stated next to it.
references:
  - type: database
    title: "DepMap Public 26Q1"
    abstract: "Source of the common-essential annotation shown beside a queried gene."
    authors:
      - name: "Broad Institute Cancer Dependency Map"
    year: 2026
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    url: "https://depmap.org/portal/"
  - type: database
    title: "TCGA RPPA, Broad GDAC Firehose run stddata__2016_01_28"
    abstract: "Reverse-phase protein array measurements behind the Protein (RPPA) tab."
    authors:
      - name: "Broad Institute TCGA Genome Data Analysis Center"
    year: 2016
    doi: "10.7908/C11G0KM9"
